WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.014
Chapter eight: AI pre-review.

00:00:02.014 --> 00:00:07.084
Every listed paper gets an automated pre-review from a team of AI agents.

00:00:07.084 --> 00:00:13.179
Its aim is to help authors and reviewers find problems early. It is advisory only.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:18.253
Every AI report carries this banner: Advisory. Generated by AI agents.

00:00:18.253 --> 00:00:19.957
Not a peer review.

00:00:19.957 --> 00:00:26.542
The AI pre-review cannot change the status of a paper, its listing, or the standing of any person.

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:30.704
The software has no path from AI output to paper status.

00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:36.139
AI content always has its own purple colour. Human reviews never use this colour.

00:00:36.139 --> 00:00:40.555
The pre-review starts automatically when a moderator lists a version.

00:00:40.555 --> 00:00:43.387
Unlisted drafts never go to AI review.

00:00:43.387 --> 00:00:48.535
Until the report is ready, the AI tab says: This paper has no AI pre-review yet.

00:00:48.535 --> 00:00:51.573
One is written after a version is listed.

00:00:51.573 --> 00:00:53.488
Four AI agents read the paper.

00:00:53.488 --> 00:00:59.868
The methodology agent looks at study design, statistics, and whether the method supports the claims.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:05.883
The literature agent looks at the references, and at how the work relates to prior work.

00:01:05.883 --> 00:01:12.539
The integrity agent looks for signs that need a human check, such as possible reuse of figures or text.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:19.595
The reproducibility agent runs the code bundle of the paper, if there is one, in a locked-down sandbox.

00:01:19.595 --> 00:01:23.640
Then a meta-review step combines the findings into one report.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.715
This step is fixed code, not an AI model.

00:01:26.715 --> 00:01:33.260
Each finding shows the agent that raised it, and its severity: info, minor, major or critical.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.141
It also shows its confidence: low, medium or high.

00:01:37.141 --> 00:01:44.933
Each finding also shows its evidence: a quotation from the paper, a numbered reference, or a line from the reproduction log.

00:01:44.933 --> 00:01:46.944
You can follow it to the source.

00:01:46.944 --> 00:01:52.496
Scholium drops findings without checkable evidence before it publishes the report.

00:01:52.496 --> 00:01:57.630
Integrity findings use careful words, and they end with: Needs a human check.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.098
The report never says fraud, or plagiarism detected.

00:02:01.098 --> 00:02:07.765
Scholium replaces such words from a model with: Possible integrity concern in the quoted text.

00:02:07.765 --> 00:02:13.459
An author of the paper can rebut a finding, to explain why it is wrong or already addressed.

00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:18.410
The rebuttal appears next to the finding. Only an author of the paper can rebut.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.285
Anyone else sees a message that says so.

00:02:21.285 --> 00:02:24.444
Reviewers can confirm a finding, or mark it wrong.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:29.771
The finding then shows Confirmed by a reviewer, or Marked wrong by a reviewer.

00:02:29.771 --> 00:02:35.688
If a paper includes code, the reproducibility agent runs it in an isolated sandbox.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:40.036
The sandbox has no network access and read-only system files.

00:02:40.036 --> 00:02:44.571
It gets one CPU, two gigabytes of memory, and ten minutes.

00:02:44.571 --> 00:02:50.411
If the server has no sandbox configured, the report says that the reproduction was not run.

00:02:50.411 --> 00:02:54.495
For node operators: one setting chooses the AI provider.

00:02:54.495 --> 00:03:00.257
The choices are Anthropic, an OpenAI-compatible service, or self-hosted Ollama.

00:03:00.257 --> 00:03:03.467
Another setting chooses the sandbox backend.

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:09.264
Hosted providers refuse unlisted drafts. The deploy guide has the details.

00:03:09.264 --> 00:03:15.746
In short: AI agents write an advisory report after listing, and every finding cites evidence.

00:03:15.746 --> 00:03:22.856
Authors can rebut, reviewers can confirm or mark a finding wrong, and the report never changes status.

00:03:22.856 --> 00:03:26.880
Next, chapter nine: moderation, appeals and reports.
